## VERDICT
**ALREADY_FIXED** (path-A). No source change this turn.

`c_sys_exec_last_arg` walks C arg text with `char_at` for comma/string/depth
classification only, then takes **one** `str_slice(args, last_start, n)`
for the last top-level span. There is no `last = last + c` / per-char
OoStr concat in the last-arg extract. `.oo` has no char stack array; the
alpha honesty for “stack buffer” is slice-once-per-span (same close as
`t1_memory.oot` M-SG3 and 7.1 `str_slice` per ident).

Source comment at `c_emit_args.oo` L121–125 already claimed this;
**source matches the claim.**

Monofile `c_emit_args.oo` = **238** lines (≤600; under soft 256).

