### Last-arg body (product host source)
File: `/home/jeryd/Projects/openOODA/ooda/oodac/c_emit_args.oo`

- L69–130: `pub fn c_sys_exec_last_arg(args: String) -> String`
- L76: `let mut last_start = 0;` — index only, no growing buffer
- L80–120: linear `while i < n` over `chars_len(args)`
- L82–97: skip `"..."` (escape-aware); L98–103: paren depth
- L104–116: top-level `,` updates `last_start` to first non-space after
- **L125:** `let out = str_slice(args, last_start, n);`  ← one slice
- L122–128: empty-span fallbacks return `args` (no rebuild)

Static grep of this function for `last = last +`, `last + c`: **no hits**.
Only string-build in the last-arg fn is the single `str_slice` at L125.

Same file L188 `out = out + c` lives in **`c_args_strip_cr`** (8.6 CR
strip), **not** 7.2 last-arg. Adjacent L153 `c_args_drop_first` already
slices remainder (M-SG4; not this OWN).

